      "timestamp": "2026-11-20T09:07:10.288+00:00",
      "timestampEdited": null,
      "callEndedTimestamp": null,
      "isPinned": false,
      "content": "Strange indeed. However, I can confirm that we don't have `67` \"ESD implant\" in our mask set.\n\nI think it's quite confusing since the ESD devices in our I/O cells are made using SAB. So this layer is for even better ESD protection? \"performance improvement\" sounds like it at least.",
      "author": {
        "id": "323371864074485771",
        "name": "mole99",
        "discriminator": "0000",
        "nickname": "Leo Moser (mole99)",
        "color": null,
        "isBot": false,
        "roles": [
          {
            "id": "1423020172595298314",
            "name": "Mod",
            "color": null,
            "position": 4
          }
        ],
        "avatarUrl": "2026-11_media/3c7c17f3225f6e56f4dccd83f14383f2-73F83.png"
